## Position-improvement playbook (striking-distance pages: position 6-17)

This is the highest-value work on the site. In order of impact:

1. **Align title/H1 with the real query language** — biggest single lever, can move 3-5 positions in two weeks.
2. **Add a 40-60 word direct-answer capsule** immediately under the heading that matches the gap query — answers first, specifics second, scope third. No hook before it.
3. **Close subtopic gaps vs. the real top 3** (from SERP research) — usually 1-2 missing subtopics, not a word-count race.
4. **Fire internal links at the page** from the site's most topically-relevant existing posts (Live URLs file) — the most underused lever, can move 2-3 positions alone.
5. **Update schema/freshness signals** — only alongside a real content change behind it, never a bare date bump.

Don't judge any of this before 30 days. Title/CTR changes show in 1-3 weeks, content/link changes take 2-6 weeks.

**Primary intent lock (unchanged from v2):** every fix serves the page's main intent and primary keyword. A query classification that would pull the page off its primary keyword is a signal to trim (C2), not to expand scope.

**Averaging trap:** before treating a position number as real, check it isn't an artifact of country/device averaging or of a second page on the site cannibalizing the same query. Fix cannibalization first if found — position often recovers on its own.

