## Content-freshness rules (for any page getting a content touch)

- Any statistic, price, or "as of [year]" claim older than ~2 years gets checked and updated or removed — don't keep it just because the trend hasn't reversed.
- A substantive update changes roughly 20-30% of the page's textual content. Bumping only the date without a real change behind it is a negative signal, not a positive one — never do a bare date bump.
- First-person, confident editorial voice ("this is the one shape that photographs better than it wears") is a real positive signal, not just a style preference — keep it, don't dilute it into third-person hedging.

