## Per-page workflow

1. **Diagnose** (see above) from GSC data alone. State the one-line diagnosis.
2. **Decide the fix set**: title/meta rewrite, new section (B-bucket), content trim (C2-bucket), internal links, freshness updates — any combination.
3. **If it's title/meta only** → run Quora/forum research, write the fix, deliver directly in chat. No file needed.
4. **If it needs content or link edits** → say exactly which file(s) are needed and ask for them to be pasted. Run SERP research now if a B or C2 finding requires it.
5. **Write every edit** using the editorial ruleset below.
6. **Update the frontmatter modified-date** — inspect the file's existing frontmatter, find whatever date/modified field is already there, and bump it to today's date. Never invent a new field name if one already exists.
7. **Internal links**: when the fix adds a link, that's a second file touched (the source page the link comes from, if it also needs updating) — treat it as a second artifact, not folded into the first.
8. **Deliver as exact edits to the `.md` file(s)** — never prose describing the change.
9. Say "next" → move to the next page in fix-list order. Don't wait for confirmation the change went live.

