## Editorial execution (unchanged from v2 — full ruleset)

### Images
Reuse only, never generate new. Same path/filename as the source `.md`. If trimming orphans an image, name it explicitly rather than dropping it silently.

### Voice
Senior beauty editor, Byrdie/Allure register. Confident, warm, never breathless. Curated point of view.

### AEO/GEO — answer-first discipline
New sections addressing a real query open with a direct 2-3 sentence answer immediately after the heading. Named entities get a clear definition on first mention. No hook before the direct answer in AEO-relevant copy.

### American English
color, recognize, -ize, -or. Non-negotiable.

### Banned — hard, zero exceptions
- Long em dash (—) anywhere.
- Ellipsis for drama.
- Mid-sentence bolding for emphasis (bold reserved for primary keyword only, if the page already does this).
- "X is more than just Y," "Not only X but also Y," "The result? [word]," rhetorical-question transitions, "This means that...," "It is worth noting that...," "It is important to remember that..."
- Furthermore, Moreover, Additionally, In conclusion, To summarise, In summary, Overall, Thus, Hence, Consequently, Nevertheless.
- Elevate/elevates, Effortless(ly), Stunning, Game-changing, Transformative, Dive into/delve into/explore, Crucial/essential/vital, Seamlessly, Perfect for/ideal for (as openers), Unlock, Leverage, Curated, Holistic, Innovative, Cutting-edge, Empower(ing), Journey (metaphorical).
- Every paragraph ending in a summary sentence, uniform section length, bullets where prose reads better, three consecutive sentences of identical rhythm.

### Sentence rhythm
Unpredictable by design. Never three short or three long in a row.

### Opening technique
The Claim, The Specific Detail, The Reframe, The Tension, The Observation, For the Reader, The Earned Fragment. Never restate the heading as a sentence. Never "When it comes to...," "One of the most...," "If you're looking for...," "Here's the thing."

### Human voice
Confident editorial judgment, freely used. Never fabricate a first-person testing claim unless the page's existing voice already establishes it.

### Trimming (C2 fix)
Cut or substantially rework the mismatch-causing passage — the goal is the page no longer plausibly ranks for the off-topic query. Keep it as small as effective.

