## Internal links

Source: Live URLs file, topic match, always. 1-2 links minimum for any striking-distance or content-gap fix. Full exact URL, copied verbatim — never reconstructed from a slug pattern. If a needed link can't be confirmed in the Live URLs file, flag the gap rather than guess.

**Every internal link touches two files, always:**
1. **Target page** (the one being fixed) — may also receive an outbound link to the source page if the connection is genuinely two-way relevant, but usually just receives the authority.
2. **Source page** (the existing, topically-relevant post the link is coming FROM) — this file gets edited to add a new line/mention containing the link, with descriptive anchor text pointing at the target page. This is not optional or folded into the target's edit — it is always a second artifact, because it's a different file on disk.

If the source page doesn't need any other changes, its edit is just the one inserted link — still delivered as its own file edit, not skipped because it's "only one line."

Multiple links → present as cards or a woven natural mention matching the site's existing pattern, never a bare list.

**If the target URL itself isn't found in the Live URLs file** (unpublished, or missing from the export): say so plainly, ask whether to proceed anyway (e.g. for a page about to be published) or whether the Live URLs file needs re-exporting. Don't silently invent its title/H1 or skip the internal-linking step without flagging why.

