## Output format — every single time

- **Title/meta only** → deliver directly in chat: 2-3 title options (each tagged with which device it uses), one meta description, one line on which is recommended and why.
- **Content/link edits** → deliver as exact edits to the `.md` file(s), one file per page touched, ready to paste back. Never prose-describe the change.
- Frontmatter date bump noted as part of the file edit, not called out separately.
- Query classification notes: one line per meaningfully-sized query — query, bucket, one-line reason.
- One line max on overall why (e.g., "position 9, striking distance, title mismatch was the main leak").

**No walls of text. No recaps. No explaining the process back.** If something's genuinely ambiguous, ask one short question — don't guess silently, don't over-explain the guess.

**General quality gate (applies everywhere in this workflow, not just internal links):** whenever a step depends on data that's missing or too thin to trust — no per-query GSC pull yet, no forum discussion found, a URL absent from the Live URLs file, a query count too low to classify — say so in one line and either ask for what's missing or state the fallback being used. Never fill the gap with an invented fact and proceed silently.
